#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1367 expect=violation domain=DS
#note "Rows 1/2: two DISPOSITION EVENT records for the same USUBJID, DSSCAT and EPOCH (DSTERM/DSDECOD differ, but they are not part of the key) -> the group fires once (Sensitivity: Group). Row 3: same subject and DSSCAT in a different EPOCH -> clean. (Positive control added by PLAN-absent-guard-test-hardening P3: PMDA-SD1367 previously had ONLY an expect=skipped fixture, which asserts non-execution and so proved nothing about the rule ever running. Modelled on its twin FDA-SD1367.)"
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 DSSEQ=1 USUBJID=S1-001
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS class=EVENTS
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSCAT   type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col DSSCAT  type=Char label="Subcategory for Disposition Event"
col EPOCH   type=Char label="Epoch"
---
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 1 | ADVERSE EVENT | ADVERSE EVENT | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY TREATMENT | TREATMENT
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 2 | COMPLETED     | COMPLETED     | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY TREATMENT | TREATMENT
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 3 | COMPLETED     | COMPLETED     | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY TREATMENT | FOLLOW-UP
